  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between Marsdekoiside A and SMMC-7721 through a series of target interactions. Marsdekoiside A is identified as a target of two different entities, HUVEC and CHP-134, both of which are targets of Isopiline. Isopiline, in turn, is a target of SMMC-7721, indicating a possible pathway where Marsdekoiside A influences Isopiline, which then affects SMMC-7721. Similarly, Marsdekoiside A is also linked to CHP-134, which also targets SMMC-7721. This suggests that Marsdekoiside A may exert its biological effects through a shared mechanism involving Isopiline, which could be a key mediator in the interaction with SMMC-7721. The varying scores across the paths indicate some level of confidence in these relationships, though the exact nature of the interaction remains uncertain. The evidence supports a possible role for Marsdekoiside A in modulating the activity of Isopiline, which ultimately affects SMMC-7721, though further experimental validation is needed to confirm these findings.",
